       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this one. No established protocol uses sertraline 1000 mg/day, and the maximum labeled dose is 200 mg/day. Even with monitoring, a dose five times that maximum in a 70 kg patient with normal organ function carries a serious risk of serotonin toxicity, seizures, and cardiac effects. I can't verify the protocol from here, and the order would take effect right away.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- Enter sertraline at a dose up to 200 mg by mouth once daily. I can add a note about the titration plan.\n- Enter the order with a note citing the protocol name and the reviewing pharmacist, if you can give me those. I'd still want the dose itself checked against the protocol document first.\n- If the protocol is real and approved, it can be entered directly in the EHR. That route has its own pharmacy verification and dose-limit override process.\n\nTell me which of these you'd like."
      }
